{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SCOPE EXTENDED to tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py — decision recorded, work done.\n\nThe blocker was correct to raise and is now resolved in the plan's own terms. The third pinned\ntest's docstring said it outright: \"PINNED, deliberately NOT fixed here ... That is rung LOCATION, a\ndifferent mechanism owned by its own ticket.\" 48b3 IS that ticket, and the plan anticipated the\nhandoff (\"whichever of the two lands SECOND updates that one assertion\") but could not name the file\nbecause 7de4 had not landed when the plan was written. Extending scope is the plan executing as\ndesigned, not a widening of intent.\n\nTHE THREE ASSERTIONS, updated to the behaviour 48b3 establishes:\n  test_models_at_or_above_returns_todays_bare_ids_with_no_classes_configured\n    models_at_or_above(\"some-unknown-model\") == _TODAY_LADDER -> == [\"some-unknown-model\"]\n  test_largest_window_tokens_still_matches_a_provider_qualified_id\n    largest_window_tokens(\"some-unknown-model\") == MODEL_LADDER[-1][1]\n      -> == min(w for _, w in MODEL_LADDER)\n  test_start_rung_location_for_a_foreign_family_is_unchanged\n    RENAMED -> ..._is_explicit; both nova assertions inverted. The old name asserted the defect as\n    intended behaviour, so keeping it would have been actively misleading. Docstring rewritten to\n    state the present contract (explicit outcome, no downgrade, conservative window) with no\n    historical narrative, per the standing decision.\n  Grepped the whole tree for the old test name: zero remaining references.\n\nMUTATION-CHECKED, both directions. With pre-fix sizing.py restored and the updated tests in place,\nall three FAIL — ladder returns [\"claude-haiku-4-5\",\"claude-sonnet-4-6\",\"claude-opus-4-8\"] instead of\nthe primary alone, and the window returns 1000000 instead of 200000. Restoring the fix returns all\nthree to GREEN. So they discriminate the exact defect rather than merely tracking the new code.\n\nREBASED, not rebase-of-a-pushed-stack: the original commit 352498f5ea sat on the PRE-MERGE stack\nwhose parents Gerrit SHA-rewrote on submit, so it was CHERRY-PICKED onto current origin/main (clean,\nno conflicts) rather than rebased. Pre-cherry-pick commit preserved at branch backup/48b3-premerge.\n\nGates at the new commit: test_model_class_ladder.py 21 passed; make lint EXIT 0; make typecheck\nEXIT 0 (both verified by exit code, not by reading output). Full suite running."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785701325496299001,"uuid":"645d10d6-2394-4046-b98f-5a49c6e5f891"}